# Proposed Updates selector

Grounding: Rankings owns its selection and header arrangement in the route; `rankings.ts` supplies the wheel geometry and formatted finance rows. `CategoryWheel` is a generic controlled button group, but every clipped button is fixed at 142×142 in a 284×284 canvas. `RankingList` requires money-specific amount, incomplete, width and sign fields. Updates already receives both complete ordered lists in SSR and presents declaration counts plus UTC dates through `ResultRow`.

Usage sketch:
```svelte
<CategoryWheel options={updateCategories} size={220} {selected}
  label="Updates category" onselect={(category) => selected = category} />
{#key selected}
  <ul class="results-list" aria-label={`${category.label} updates`}>
    <!-- Existing ResultRow, identity/count/date content -->
  </ul>
{/key}
```

Types and ownership:
```ts
// lib/updates.ts
export type UpdateCategory = 'members' | 'companies';
export const updateCategories: CategoryWheelOption<UpdateCategory>[];
// Route
let selected = $state<UpdateCategory>('members');
const rows = $derived(data.updates?.[selected] ?? []);
```
No additional row model or adapter: the existing `EntityUpdate` retains the data we actually display. The selected category determines the icon, URL prefix and accent with an exhaustive two-category mapping. Keep the server loader unchanged.

Choose existing native `ResultRow` composition. Reusing `RankingList` would put declaration counts or dates into `amount` and require fake financial flags and bars. A new shared UpdatesList would add a component boundary for a single consumer without removing meaningful complexity.

Mirror the Rankings intro layout: heading and existing month at left, controlled wheel at right; one full-width result board below; stacked intro on narrow screens. Remove the now-redundant category section headings; accessible selector/list labels retain identity.

Geometry: reuse the existing MPs top-left and Companies bottom-right quadrant options, narrowed explicitly to `UpdateCategory`. Both paths and button hit regions remain valid, with no irrelevant categories. This is the smallest safe selector change and preserves familiar category positions. Its tradeoff is a visibly sparse wheel. If a filled two-sector disc is mandatory, extend CategoryWheel with typed button bounds and supply genuine 142×284 semicircles; do not draw semicircles inside the current 142×142 buttons.

Animation: add a feature-authored row class and route-local global selector scoped under the updates list. A 220ms translateY(6px→0) entry with capped stagger (e.g. min(index, 4)×20ms) runs on initial insertion and category replacement. Keep opacity at 1 so SSR content remains visible immediately; no timer, spinner, async loading state or artificial delay. Reduced-motion disables the animation. Prefer a CSS custom delay on a native wrapper/list row only if ResultRow can accept it naturally; otherwise use identical simultaneous entry, avoiding a new prop solely for stagger.

Verification: preserve order, all counts, UTC dates and URLs; test default MPs, Companies switch, pressed states, keyboard activation, empty/error states, reduced motion, responsive overflow and SSR content without JS. Run check/build/affected Playwright; capture desktop PR screenshots. No backend or financial semantics change.
